\n\nUnknown-but-natural:\n\nrare radio astronomy phenomena we haven’t catalogued yet\n\nExtraterrestrial intelligence:\n\nlogically possible\n\nbut not supported by independent corroboration\n\nSo the real structure is:\n\nmultiple competing generative models, none uniquely selected by the data\n\nThat is NOT the same as “cannot be explained.”\n\nIt is:\n\nunderdetermined inference problem\n\n4. The deeper truth (this is the part you’re circling)\n\nYou’re asking:\n\n“How do you confirm when you only get one shot at reality?”\n\nAnd the uncomfortable answer","chars":3959,"fullLen":3959,"chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a378333-ebe8-83e8-a301-dfd0ee99efb1","_account":"chatgpt.com","_chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a378333-ebe8-83e8-a301-dfd0ee99efb1"},"source":"userscript-chatgpt","causedBy":"6cf71c1d-6316-4d63-aab3-48468eced213","ts":1782040864019,"_rowId":60139,"_ts":1782040864019},{"uuid":"0e3562cd-c0a6-44be-8915-92e0a53e3c53","type":"guardian.job.stream","payload":{"jobId":"6cf71c1d-6316-4d63-aab3-48468eced213","provider":"chatgpt","text":"Yeah—this is exactly where the “model-relative anomaly” idea gets stress-tested, because cases like the Wow! Signal feel like they resist clean closure.\n\nLet’s use it properly, not mystify it.\n\n1. What the Wow! Signal actually is (ground truth)\n\nThe Wow! Signal was:\n\ndetected once (1977, Ohio State “Big Ear” radio telescope)\n\nlasted ~72 seconds\n\nnarrowband radio spike\n\nlooked like something non-natural at first glance\n\nnever reliably re-detected in the same form\n\nSo yes—it looks like a clean “open loop.”\n\nBut scientifically, it’s classified as:\n\nan unconfirmed transient radio anomaly\n\nNot “alien signal,” not “resolved natural source.”\n\n2. Why it feels like an “uncloseable loop”\n\nYou’re hitting something real here: single-observation events break our closure instincts.\n\nBecause normally science relies on:\n\nrepeatability\n\nindependent verification\n\ncontrolled conditions\n\nThe Wow signal violat