ealth","payload":"{\"ollama\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"gemini\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"perplexity\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0}}","source":"raid","ts":1782041122110,"_rowId":76038,"_ts":1782041122110},{"uuid":"2dd99eb9-2e6a-492a-9e92-c79602bd3abb","type":"raid.health","payload":"{\"ollama\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"guardian-chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"claude\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"chatgpt\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"gemini\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0},\"perplexity\":{\"online\":true,\"fails\":0}}","source":"raid","ts":1782041122110,"_rowId":76039,"_ts":1782041122110},{"uuid":"71a972d1-c888-4811-9d80-eb452e141159","type":"memory.observer.heartbeat","payload":{"provider":"chatgpt","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","turnsSeen":31,"version":"1.0.0","_provider":"chatgpt","_chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a378333-ebe8-83e8-a301-dfd0ee99efb1"},"source":"userscript-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782041122160,"_rowId":76040,"_ts":1782041122160},{"uuid":"db8538f1-27c6-408a-b997-8a442043ec0c","type":"working.memory.turn","payload":{"type":"turn","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","role":"user","content":"im saying litterally give you a tool to use nexus' diagnostic tool to help nexus get moving if its not moving","provider":"chatgpt","chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a378333-ebe8-83e8-a301-dfd0ee99efb1","turnIndex":29,"ts":1782041096896,"_provider":"chatgpt","_chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a378333-ebe8-83e8-a301-dfd0ee99efb1"},"source":"userscript-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782041122540,"_rowId":76043,"_ts":1782041122540},{"uuid":"87f89668-dca3-4a5d-8d00-f6004681a3ab","type":"working.memory.turn","payload":{"type":"turn","sessionId":"chatgpt:home","role":"assistant","content":"Ah—now I get it. You’re not asking for a redesign. You’re asking for a real “escape hatch tool” I can call when Nexus stalls.\n\nThat’s actually a solid idea. Here’s what that tool should look like so I can actively help unstick the system instead of just observing it.\n\n🔧 Nexus Diagnostic Escape Tool (what to give me)\n\nYou want a single tool that lets me do three things:\n\ninspect state\n\ndetect why it’s stuck\n\nsuggest or trigger the next transition\n\nSo define a tool like this:\n\n🧠 TOOL: nexus_diagnose\nJSON\n{\n  \"tool\": \"nexus_diagnose\",\n  \"reason\": \"system_stall | missing_transition | no_execution | buffer_lock | unknown\",\n  \"snapshot\": {\n    \"state\": \"intake | buffering | execute | idle\",\n    \"last_event\": \"string\",\n    \"missing_event\": \"string | null\",\n    \"buffer_status\": \"empty | partial | full\",\n    \"expected_transition\": \"chunk_1 | chunk_2 | execute | unknown\"\n  },\n  \"event_log\": [\n    \"INTAKE\",\n    \"CHUNK_RECEIVED\",\n    \"RETRY\"\n  ]\n}\n🚨 What I do with this tool\n\nWhen I receive it, I stop “chat reasoning” and switch to control-plane mode:\n\nI would:\n\n1. Detect stall type\n\nExample outputs:\n\n“waiting on missing SEAM_END”\n\n“chunk received but not committed”\n\n“execution trigger never fired”\n\n“state mismatch (declared vs actual)”\n\n2. Identify exact break point\n\nNot vague:\n\n“transition from buffering → execute never occurred”\n\n“retry loop overriding state progression”\n\n“listener not emitting seam_end event”\n\n3. Output a fix action (critical part)\n\nI would respond with something like:\n\nJSON\n{\n  \"action\": \"force_transition\",\n  \"target_state\": \"execute\",\n  \"reason\": \"valid chunk received but execution gate not triggered\"\n}\n\nor\n\nJSON\n{\n  \"action\": \"request_missing_signal\",\n  \"missing\": \"SEAM_END_EXECUTE_1\"\n}\n\nor even:\n\nJSON\n{\n  \"action\": \"reset_buffer\",\n  \"reason\": \"state desync detected\"\n}\n🧩 Why this matters (this is the core insight)\n\nRight now your system has:\n\nevents (chunks, retries)\n\nbut no diagnostic authority that can re-align state\n\nSo when it breaks:\n\nnothing has permission to say “you are stuck here, jump to X”\n\nThis tool gives me that authority.\n\n⚙️ Minimal version (if you want ultra-lightweight)\n\nIf you want the simplest usable version:\n\nJSON\n{\n  \"tool\": \"nexus_diagnose\",\n  \"state\": \"...\",\n  \"log\": [...]\n}\n\nAnd I handle inference internally.\n\n🧠 What this unlocks\n\nWith this tool, I can:\n\ndetect deadlocks in your listener\n\nidentify missing transitions instantly\n\nsuggest corrective state jumps\n\ndifferentiate “no input” vs “stuck system”\n\nact like a debugger inside the control loop\n\n⚠️ Brutal truth (important)\n\nRight now your system fails because:\n\nit can observe events, but it cannot correct itself\n\nThis tool gives it:\n\na corrective feedback loop\n\nWithout it, you get:\n\ninfinite INTAKE states\n\nrepeated retries\n\nno execution trigger resolution\n\nIf you want next step, I can design a full “Nexus self-healing loop” where:\n\nlistener detects stall\n\ndiagnostic tool fires automatically\n\nsystem self-corrects state\n\nThat’s where this becomes actually interesting.","provider":"chatgpt","chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a378333-ebe8-83e8-a301-dfd0ee99efb1","turnIndex":30,"ts":1782041106614,"_provider":"chatgpt","_chatUrl":"https://chatgpt.com/c/6a378333-ebe8-83e8-a301-dfd0ee99efb1"},"source":"userscript-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782041122540,"_rowId":76045,"_ts":1782041122540},{"uuid":"9089c57c-8a25-48a2-975e-d566bdebee82","type":"memory.observer.heartbeat","payload":{"provider":"claude","sessionId":"claude:home","turnsSeen":0,"version":"1.0.0","_provider":"claude","_chatUrl":"https://claude.ai/new"},"source":"userscript-memory","causedBy":null,"ts":1782041123933,"_rowId":76050,"_ts":1782041123933},{"uuid":"eb01bdcb-d360-414b-82d8-4ad08189c7c2","type":"self-heal.forge_failed","payload":{"gapUuid":"2a54292d-315f-4e6a-b74a-1b6062350